# ADR 0004: Modular folder structure (Core / Training / Nutrition)

**Date:** 2026-08-02
**Status:** Accepted

## Context
FORGE will ship with training features in v1 and nutrition features 
later. Cross-cutting concerns (body weight, HealthKit, settings) 
belong to neither module exclusively.

## Decision
Organise the Xcode project by folder into three top-level areas:
- `Core/` — shared entities and services (BodyWeight, HealthKit 
  wrapper, Settings, Notifications)
- `Training/` — programs, sessions, logging, Watch integration
- `Nutrition/` — meals, meal logging (stubs only in v1)

Use folders, not Swift Package Manager modules. Migrating to SPM 
modules later is possible if compile times or boundaries demand it.

## Alternatives considered
- **Flat structure:** Fine for tiny apps; becomes a mess quickly.
- **SPM modules from day one:** Overengineered for a solo project; 
  adds friction to every refactor.

## Consequences
- Clear namespacing from the start.
- Body weight and HealthKit access sit in Core, shared by both 
  modules.
- Nutrition can be built without touching Training code.
